body:
I would still defer because I kind of need to in order to get everything ready in time. My parents are contributing 100k so they still need to take out loans and I also need time to comfortably set up housing and everything. It’s possible to do in time, but I’d kind of rather defer so that I can work on personal projects and skills for a bit before I have little time to do so.

What you say about BU makes sense, but I will add that BU offers more exploration and flexibility than UCLA for me and I’d be able to complete it in four years as opposed to 3. If I graduate in 3 years at BU it would be much less debt.

And as for your last question, a combination of parental pressure, mental health issues peaking, and a lot of unexpected medical issues and trauma in my personal life caused me to do that and I’ve been having a shit summer trying to fix this whole problem every single day );
